Breadslicer support crates
==========================

bread-support-geom, bread-support-model, bread-support-mesh, bread-support-placement, bread-support-bracing
and bread-support-pipeline (with bread-support-session, which runs them for a scene).

The support system of these crates was first ported to Rust from the support
system of:

  DragonFruit, Open Resin Alliance and contributors
  https://github.com/Open-Resin-Alliance/DragonFruit
  SynrgStudio private downstream revision f331fc555abb31c4bcb28d1a358edb887f0afe07

DragonFruit is licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later. The port has since been rewritten
module by module as Breadslicer's own code, giving the same supports, and split
into these crates. They remain under AGPL-3.0-or-later. SoulCrafted Slicer is
itself AGPL-3.0.

The geometry (vectors, matrices, rays, triangles, extrusion), the BVH and the
polygon booleans are Breadslicer's own code, on glam, earcutr and i_overlay
(MIT/Apache-2.0, ISC).
